 # User Flow Tree
 
+## Engineering39 granted routine evidence
+
+- A synthetic owner records a use with a confirmed bottle observation and later retracts the use. In professional pre-visit review, select Recorded use or Formula observations under the respective current grant. Recorded use shows the original phase and version without label details. Formula observations show the retained bottle observation and its original recorded time. After retraction, an older review must request a fresh source. The refreshed report identifies the earlier use as retracted. Missing original receipts, an unconfirmed archive checkpoint, withdrawn grants and retired health epochs refuse.
+- Synthetic owner applies a routine on mobile and explicitly clears that version. Each acknowledged original enters encrypted custody under its own immutable receipt. A professional with a current pre-visit routine grant can load those exact versions and select either for review or export. A clear is presented as the owner's plan decision.
+- Refresh after a selected receipt changes. A stale reviewed source, substituted receipt, ungranted field, grant withdrawal or tombstoned epoch must refuse. At 375×667, 390×844 and 430×932, verify keyboard selection, cancel, review, export, focus and clear wording. Also verify the default professional API returns 503 with no trusted source configured.
+- In the local custody fixture, terminate the writer before commit and after commit but before reply. Reopen from a fresh process, retry the same original and verify the exact outcome. Reinsert a saved synthetic envelope after completed tombstoned erasure. Run a new authorized recheck and verify the removal and original receipt through restart.
+
 ## Engineering38 connected custody and recovery
 
 - If a private brief save is unconfirmed, review the brief and return to editing. Retry the original save explicitly. The submitted text can be saved while newer typing stays in the editor until the owner chooses which text to keep.
